# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaPTYTests` target, and SwiftPM
# fails to resolve if the directory is missing. Git does not track empty
# directories, so this file is what keeps it alive across a clone. Delete it once
# there is a real test file here.
#
# What belongs here (see docs/testing.md):
#
#   - Spawning real processes. `/bin/echo` and assert the output and exit code;
#     `cat` and assert a write round-trips.
#   - The controlling terminal actually works: run something that opens
#     `/dev/tty`, and assert Ctrl-C (0x03) delivers SIGINT. This is the test that
#     would have caught the `posix_spawn` mistake described in
#     `PseudoTerminal.swift`.
#   - Resize delivers SIGWINCH, and `ws_xpixel`/`ws_ypixel` survive the round trip.
#   - Signals reach the process GROUP: spawn a shell that spawns a child, kill the
#     group, assert the grandchild died too.
#   - Back-pressure: flood the PTY and assert memory stays bounded and no bytes
#     are lost. Bytes must never be dropped — see `ByteStream.swift`.
#   - Teardown ordering: closing the fd in the DispatchIO cleanup handler rather
#     than before, so we never hit `EV_VANISHED`.
